   read:'Pew has asked the control question twice: 59% (2024), then 57% (2025), said not too much or none. Two readings are not a trend, and the change is within survey noise. A Dutch panel asks whether people know how to influence what AI recommends to them; a Finnish panel follows attitudes to AI on the same people. Concern about AI (grey) stepped up in 2023 and has been flat since; it is a mood, not a measure of lost agency.',
